{"parentUuid":"1007f274-c3c5-44a9-b51d-2bdf41237cf9","isSidechain":false,"type":"system","subtype":"away_summary","content":"We built the `entire stats` command and cleaned it up via /simplify. Next step: add unit tests for the computation and rendering logic.","timestamp":"2026-04-21T14:48:37.913Z","uuid":"edb24848-d764-4180-a7b5-7bf1c4268606","isMeta":false,"userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"06af762d-fb18-426b-8b89-e1a11aba933b","version":"2.1.104","gitBranch":"soph/stats","slug":"adaptive-wiggling-lemon"}
{"parentUuid":"edb24848-d764-4180-a7b5-7bf1c4268606","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"2590c1d3-f21b-4bc4-88fb-ced0729195e0","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"**Findings**\n\n1. Medium: the `ITERATION` card is labeled as “Avg steps/checkpoint”, but the value is actually computed from `session_count`, not `steps`. That means the CLI can show a materially wrong metric whenever checkpoints have multiple steps in one session. See [stats_cmd.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/stats_cmd.go:143), [stats_cmd.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/stats_cmd.go:152), [stats_types.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/stats_types.go:69), and [stats_render.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/stats_render.go:119).\n\n2. Medium: commit agent badges ignore the singular `agent` field entirely. The API model includes both `agent` and `agents`, but `uniqueCommitAgents` only reads `Agents`. If the backend returns only `agent` for some rows, the commit list silently drops agent attribution. See [stats_types.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/stats_types.go:36) and [stats_render.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/stats_render.go:346).\n\n3. Low: commits with missing or unparsable dates are grouped under `\"unknown\"` and then reverse-sorted with real dates. Lexicographically, `\"unknown\"` sorts above `2026-…`, so bad data bubbles to the top of the “recent commits” section. See [stats_cmd.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments/cmd/entire/cli/stats_cmd.go:246).\n\n**Tests I’d add**\n\nThere are currently no `stats` tests in `cmd/entire/cli/`. I’d add them in two files:\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/stats_cmd_test.go`\n- `cmd/entire/cli/stats_render_test.go`\n\nMost valuable cases:\n\n- `computeContributionStats`\n  - verifies throughput uses tokens\n  - verifies iteration uses the intended field\n  - verifies continuity uses max `steps`\n  - nil token/session/step fields default correctly\n\n- `computeStreaks`\n  - dedupes multiple timestamps on one day\n  - handles invalid timestamps\n  - current streak starts from today or yesterday only\n\n- `normalizeAgentString`\n  - `Claude Code`, `copilot-cli`, `factoryai-droid`, unknown values\n\n- `groupCommitsByDay`\n  - valid dates sort newest first\n  - `unknown` bucket is forced last\n\n- `uniqueCommitAgents` / `renderCommitList`\n  - falls back to `agent` when `agents` is empty\n  - dedupes and sorts badges\n  - handles nil commit message, singular/plural file/checkpoint wording\n\n- `formatCommitDate`\n  - today\n  - yesterday\n  - older date\n  - future date should not be labeled today/yesterday\n\n**Recommendation**\n\nYes, add more tests here. The highest ROI is pure table-driven coverage around the new stats helpers and renderer, because almost all of this logic is deterministic and currently unprotected. If you want command-level coverage too, I’d first make `runStats` accept an injectable client factory so login failure and API error paths can be tested cleanly."},"uuid":"6835e2a6-a53c-4272-81f8-0b4bb6a5dc8a","timestamp":"2026-04-21T14:58:34.497Z","permissionMode":"acceptEdits","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli_experiments","sessionId":"06af762d-fb18-426b-8b89-e1a11aba933b","version":"2.1.104","gitBranch":"soph/stats","slug":"adaptive-wiggling-lemon"}
